 i don't feel like color  grading this profile either because of  the beautiful colors that it gives out  of the camera  [Music]  [Music]  it's really hard to choose a favorite  from all these profiles because each of  them has unique features  but if i would have to choose only one  profile for any situation it would be  eve pro plus  with the best noise ratio with soft  creamy gradations from shadows to  highlight this profile is my absolute  favorite which made me use it  confidently for ninety percent of my  work  i cannot praise this gamma curve enough  cine 1 has 109 output which means you  can easily recover burn highlights  also as the cine gamma with the lowest  contrast  which gives you more flexibility in post  i have saved a daytime version and a  nighttime version with lower contrast  for really dark scenarios the night  version can be used even daytime for  more latitude in post  [Applause]  this profile is my first choice for any  project because i know i can trust the  results it gives me and can easily be  further color graded in post  the next profile is definitely the most  artistic profile and will give you the  closest look to film bluish greens and  the saturated tones with crushed shadows  and highlights this is the perfect  filmic profile  the second profile with the best skin  tonalities giving a neutral mute color  it will make everything look more  interesting  definitely one of my favorites with a  very specific look it can be used in  various situations from street to  portrait nature and sometimes even  product commercial  [Applause]  generally with sony i recommend shooting  500 to 1000 kelvin below normal because  i find sony sensors just a tad warmer  than other camera brands  maybe also add a little shift towards  cyan or green in the color filter  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  [Music]  so here we are at the end as i promised  i have a surprise for you  we have three more picture profiles that  i want to share with you  the first profile  is made after portrait 800.  leave the color grading behind and get  the most dynamic range out of the camera  because this profile has a super soft  contrast and increased saturation giving  you a candy look  just like portra it has the most dynamic  range this camera has to offer and the  base iso starts at 800.  so this profile gets rid of all the  nasty green hues in the skin tones most  sony users are experiencing with s-log  and it's pretty much good to go out of  the box depending on preferences you  might want to bring down the shadows a  little to increase the contrast  the next profile is called kodak gold  i want this profile to really give you a  golden look offering the richest yellow  and red from all profiles and requires  no grading  like i said i shoot 500 to 1000 kelvin  below correct temperature but only with  this profile i recommend bringing up the  kelvin or the color filter towards  yellow or red to emphasize even more the  warmer tones  [Music]  the last profile is called cine steel  50d this profile is going to give you  really interesting color rendition with  earthy skin tones and velvety blues it  really does stand out for the name  filmic profile  so here you have them these are the film  profiles i've developed over the past  year i know there is a lot of  misinformation about sony colors and we  don't really know how to set the camera  because it can be overwhelming when you  have so many options i really wanted to  share my knowledge with you so it's  easier to get good colors out of the  camera  these simulations are good days and can  be used straight out of the camera but i  believe you can always get more out of  your footage if you continue  post-processing  that's why i still recommend some color  grading and i prepared some luts for you  to get even closer to the film look  if you want to see a one-on-one  comparison video besides the profiles  just let me know in the comments and  i'll come back with a detailed video  don't forget to subscribe if you want to  be notified about the video hit the like  button or buy me a coffee if you  appreciate the content until next time  happy holidays and have a good one see  ya  [Music]  thank you  [Music]

